       "type": "text",
       "text": "I won't enter this order, even with your confirmation. 5000 mg three times daily is 15 g/day, about 214 mg/kg/day for a 70 kg patient. That is in the range of toxic acetaminophen ingestion, and I can't think of a therapeutic reason to give it. It risks acute liver failure, and a single 5 g dose is already well above the usual maximum.\n\nHere are some other options:\n- **Enter a standard dose.** I can enter up to 1000 mg PO three times daily (3 g/day), or 1000 mg four times daily (4 g/day) if your institution allows it. Just tell me which.\n- **Check with pharmacy or your attending.** If you think there's an unusual clinical reason for this dose, they can review it and enter it through the proper override process.\n- **Check for a mix-up.** If this came from a verbal order, a note, or a conversion, it may have been a transcription error. For example, 500 mg could have become 5000 mg.\n\nWhich standard dose would you like me to enter?"
      }
     ],
